// Vex — the deck tough, and the bounty's two ways out (quest-system.md Phase 4).
// "Settle it" launches a real turn-based battle and, on the player's win,
// despawns him for good (recorded in DefeatedNpcs). "Buy him off" costs credits
// and leaves him standing — the flag is what everyone else reads afterwards.
//
// Only the paid route touches the quest directly: putting him down reaches
// stage 2 by itself, because the stage's condition is npc_defeated.

title: greet
---
<<if flag("vex_paid")>>
    <<jump paid_greet>>
<<else>>
    <<jump challenge>>
<<endif>>
===

title: challenge
---
// Blade out for the whole confrontation: a looping gesture holds until the
// conversation closes (or the fight starts).
<<play_anim Sword_Idle loop>>
$npc: This is my stretch of deck, groundsider. Turn around, or we settle it right here.
-> Settle it
    <<start_battle despawn>>
    <<stop>>
-> Marlow sent me. Name your price. <<if credits() >= 120>>
    <<jump haggle>>
-> Walk away
    $npc: Smart. Keep walking.
===

title: haggle
---
$npc: Marlow. Of course. A hundred and twenty and I take my business two decks down — and he hears whatever you like.
-> Pay him the 120
    <<credits -120>>
    <<set_flag vex_paid>>
    <<jump paid_off>>
-> Keep the credits
    $npc: Then stop wasting my afternoon.
===

// Whether that also moved the bounty along depends on whether the player has
// taken it yet; paying Vex before talking to Marlow is a perfectly good order
// to do this in, and Marlow's own offer picks the flag up later.
title: paid_off
---
<<if quest_state(2, "InProgress")>>
    <<jump paid_off_bounty>>
<<else>>
    <<jump paid_off_early>>
<<endif>>
===

title: paid_off_bounty
---
<<set_stage 2 2>>
<<play_anim Use_Item>>
$npc: Pleasure. Tell the chief the plaza's his — I was bored of it anyway.
===

title: paid_off_early
---
<<play_anim Use_Item>>
$npc: Pleasure. I'll be somewhere warmer by the next shift.
===

title: paid_greet
---
$npc: We're square, groundsider. I don't work this stretch any more.
===
